{
 "_doc": "Per-model split of the fal turrets (tools/rig/prep_turret.py). All points are in the model's own glTF frame as Trellis made it (a unit box, Y up). forward: the way the gun points (flat). yaw_y: everything above this height swivels. pitch: the gun's elevation pivot; gun_min_y: the gun is everything swivelling above this height (optionally gun_box). spin: box of parts that spin, with their axis point and axis. height: the finished turret's height in metres. Optional: centre [x, z] (swivel about this point for a model made off-centre); base_box: a list of boxes that stay on the base (loose props); gun_box may be a list of boxes; gun_tilt_deg: how far the gun as made points nose-up (negative: nose-down), levelled about the pitch pivot. head_box: a list of boxes that swivel but never pitch (carriage cheeks or a stand hugging the gun). yaw_pivot_y: the swivel's height when it isn't yaw_y (the game sights from the swivel, so a carriage that turns from its wheels still sights from its top).",
